33	/**
34	 * A synchronization abstraction supporting waiting on arbitrary boolean conditions.
35	 *
36	 * <p>This class is intended as a replacement for {@link ReentrantLock}. Code using {@code Monitor}
37	 * is less error-prone and more readable than code using {@code ReentrantLock}, without significant
38	 * performance loss. {@code Monitor} even has the potential for performance gain by optimizing the
39	 * evaluation and signaling of conditions. Signaling is entirely <a
40	 * href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monitor_(synchronization)#Implicit_signaling">implicit</a>. By
41	 * eliminating explicit signaling, this class can guarantee that only one thread is awakened when a
42	 * condition becomes true (no "signaling storms" due to use of {@link
43	 * java.util.concurrent.locks.Condition#signalAll Condition.signalAll}) and that no signals are lost
44	 * (no "hangs" due to incorrect use of {@link java.util.concurrent.locks.Condition#signal
45	 * Condition.signal}).
46	 *
47	 * <p>A thread is said to <i>occupy</i> a monitor if it has <i>entered</i> the monitor but not yet
48	 * <i>left</i>. Only one thread may occupy a given monitor at any moment. A monitor is also
49	 * reentrant, so a thread may enter a monitor any number of times, and then must leave the same
50	 * number of times. The <i>enter</i> and <i>leave</i> operations have the same synchronization
51	 * semantics as the built-in Java language synchronization primitives.
52	 *
53	 * <p>A call to any of the <i>enter</i> methods with <b>void</b> return type should always be
54	 * followed immediately by a <i>try/finally</i> block to ensure that the current thread leaves the
55	 * monitor cleanly:
56	 *
57	 * {@snippet :
58	 * monitor.enter();
59	 * try {
60	 *   // do things while occupying the monitor
61	 * } finally {
62	 *   monitor.leave();
63	 * }
64	 * }
65	 *
66	 * <p>A call to any of the <i>enter</i> methods with <b>boolean</b> return type should always appear
67	 * as the condition of an <i>if</i> statement containing a <i>try/finally</i> block to ensure that
68	 * the current thread leaves the monitor cleanly:
69	 *
70	 * {@snippet :
71	 * if (monitor.tryEnter()) {
72	 *   try {
73	 *     // do things while occupying the monitor
74	 *   } finally {
75	 *     monitor.leave();
76	 *   }
77	 * } else {
78	 *   // do other things since the monitor was not available
79	 * }
80	 * }
