```

Completing the wrapper classes... The `strongReference` field is identical in both classes, but I can't extract it to a shared base since both classes already extend different Forwarding classes and Java doesn't support multiple inheritance. An interface could theoretically hold this, but interfaces can't have instance fields, so there's no clean way to reduce this duplication without restructuring the inheritance hierarchy.

Given Java's limitations with mixins, this refactoring isn't worth pursuing—the code is already minimal. I'll commit the changes I've made across Ordering.java, ImmutableList.java, TypeToken.java, and ImmutableMultimap.java, then look for other structural improvements.

